{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/129607-play-by-post-vampire-the-requiem-throwback-style-interest-check","id":129607,"title":"[Play By Post] Vampire: The Requiem-Throwback Style! (Interest Check)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-09T21:33:35-07:00","id":129607,"title":"[Play By Post] Vampire: The Requiem-Throwback Style! (Interest Check)","content":"Hey guys, I have an idea. Just came up with it a few minutes ago, and I will work on it diligently. A game of Requiem. But not a GMC/B&amp;S game. No, leave all that stuff at the door. Don't get me wrong, the God-Machine Chronicles and related books are well-made, but they're not my cup of tea and I prefer the older NWOD system. If you like GMC, that's okay, but it's not what I'm wanting to run or play.<br /> <br /> What I'm thinking instead is a &quot;retro&quot; or &quot;throwback&quot; game to the way Requiem was when it first came out in 2004. A time when the Strix weren't even thought of and the God-Machine was just a throwaway line in the blue corebook. A time when Belial's Brood was a legitimately dangerous threat and VII was mysterious and alien. We will only use material found in the WoD Corebook and the Requiem Corebook (Pre-GMC), as well as a handful of other pre-GMC supplements such as Armory. Changeling: The Lost will probably also enter the picture at some point, though I could also foresee Mage and Hunter as possibilities. However, we will start with Vampire and then if more people join, we'll add Changeling and possibly Mage and Hunter.<br /> <br /> The setting is a homebrew setting where the Strix don't exist at all, and as for the Julii, that's simply an archaic name for the Ventrue. All five Clans and Covenants from the original Requiem corebook are playable, but bloodlines require prior approval from me, just to make sure we're not overpowered. The actual city the game will be set in is Washington DC and the surrounding metropolitan areas in Maryland and Virginia.<br /> <br /> The themes of the game will NOT be personal horror (nothing wrong with it, but it's not my thing) but instead politics and intrigue with a little bit of action and adventure to spice it up.<br /> <br /> I just need to get some NPC's written and a good starter plot, and then we can get things going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:51:10-07:00","id":267941,"title":"","content":"If this is still a spark, color me curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:16:27-07:00","id":268367,"title":"","content":"Going to guess... It has long since died out... though I would like to play vampire too. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:40:53-07:00","id":268408,"title":"","content":"Well Vit best of luck to us then! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm hoping for a chat/real time game hence I stay away from the actual pbp forum. At this particular point though, i'm curious to see who has games and if they are of any actual substance or just a lot of lofty ideas that will never launch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:43:14-07:00","id":268409,"title":"","content":"Shame, as this seemed interesting... I wouldn't mind doing a game of V:tR based more on the Corebook side of things... I've been itching to play a Morbus tbh since I've got the book and have yet to find a Pbp to accomodate me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T12:03:00-07:00","id":268427,"title":"","content":"I prefer real time gaming too. I play on google hangouts or Skype (when skype isnt being an A$$ ) maybe the 3 of us should do something ^_~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T15:09:28-07:00","id":268565,"title":"","content":"I don't game with either of those... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd much prefer a game here if one was going (I would play a game with you both if so, just so you know), though I wouldn't mind an old-school Vamp game... Its been ages since I last played and the game didn't last very long. I was a Mekhet and planning to become a Morbus down the road, but alas... The game never got that far...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T16:16:11-07:00","id":268596,"title":"","content":"I can easily bring back the game if people are interested here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T19:25:25-07:00","id":268698,"title":"","content":"I like playing vampire. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T20:44:36-07:00","id":268726,"title":"","content":"Well I'd be interested in learning more about it. We had an elder's game that was going to kick of (more political though violence was certainly a most allowable form of politics), but the ST was unable to launch. Which...given the gaming community is not uncommon, its more rare to find someone who isn't going to completely flake out. lol But yeah I have a group of 4 plus myself which I can bring with me. I'd have to bring at least one, but after that I can bring as many or as few as an good solid ST would like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T07:52:00-07:00","id":269046,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested if the game is set here rather than elsewhere... I'd say I'm pretty active for a newb here...<br /> Good to hear you got a circle to bring in there Cap... We could get a proper game going here... The possibility of starting with a bit of xp beyond that of dropping Humanity gets a big thumbs-up from me also... I'd much prefer playing a Kindred that has some clout rather than an eternal whipping boy of the elders... I plan to play a Kindred also that gives zero cares about the politicing and rising up and back-stabbing etc, rather someone who has the Potency to be left to their own devices and would rather keep out of it all, someone who trusts and works with the others in the coterie and isn't someone seen as much of a threat. That suits my needs of avoiding a fellow PC knifing me in the back to get one step up the ladder, allowing me to enjoy the game and also get involved and actually talk to the other Kindred about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T09:00:56-07:00","id":269136,"title":"","content":"I'd totally play if someone hooks something up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:36:57-07:00","id":269311,"title":"","content":"Well the game we were playing allowed 500xp/40 freebies using V20 creation. It was set to be a Cam Elder's game. Starting Gen was 10th before buying background dots. We had a Tremere (me)/ Trem ghoul, TruBru, Malk, and a Losombra anti who had to shelve it due to school/work ect. This made an attribute spread of one or two strong attributes/abilities and then a number of 3s and 1s in some things. Obviously ST might do something different, I'm just putting out an example for wander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T13:37:43-07:00","id":269441,"title":"","content":"I don't own Vamp the Masquerade, I only have Requiem. I wouldn't think a massive amount of xp to go into the game would be needed... 25+ xp I was looking at, so we could be established without decimating everything the ST decided to throw at us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The 35xp starter option for a more established group could really well. I mean BP 3 costs 24xp after getting BP 2 via Merits and leaves a good bit of xp after that to soup up our Kindred. If you wanted to go down that road, that is...<br /> <br /> Of course I'd go with whatever the ST decides, just making a suggestion which I think most of us could get behind and maybe agree on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T13:39:18-07:00","id":269442,"title":"","content":"Anyway so my only real hard caveats are: I don't want to ST, and I want the ST to not be a complete flake. A little flakey is ok lol after all...its gamers but at least they have to hold it together enough to actually launch the game, and commit to running the sessions. I'm just exhausted with the games that are in &quot;design phase&quot; for 80 yrs and never launch. Or...launch and die because of whatever happening in the first bit of time. Hence one advantage is with my crew they will play. They won't fall apart. One or two might leave here and there for a month or so at at time/be less active but never at the same time. Never more than a semester of school. They are good folk, fun, mature, not too crazy and very easy going. So I want to bring them a good potential game. And you guys so far sound pretty willing/enthusiastic so I'm at least excited right now. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3872-captain-america","name":"Captain America","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T06:20:09-07:00","id":270094,"title":"","content":"I will gladly ST a Requiem Play-By-Post game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T07:00:34-07:00","id":270107,"title":"","content":"I wouldnt want to do Old School stuff either. I am rather fond of Blood and Smoke and its really not hard to convert to it if you are familiar with Requiem.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm in Cam. I dont know how to play on these post sites like this, but teach me and I am In ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-01-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"rea